# ✦ Eventora

**Create. Manage. Celebrate.**

Eventora is a PHP and MySQL event management website. Anyone can browse public events. Registered users can create public or private events, book seats, and manage guests from their own dashboard. An admin panel lets the website owner control users, events, bookings and the content of the site itself.

---

## Features

### For visitors
- Landing page with an image slider, upcoming public events, categories and a "How it works" section.
- Browse and search public events.
- Register and log in.

### For logged-in users
- **Dashboard** with live counters, upcoming bookings, upcoming events and suggested events.
- **Create events** as public or private.
- **Edit events** (title, category, date, time, location, capacity, visibility, description). Only the owner or an admin can edit, and capacity cannot go below the seats already confirmed.
- **Booking requests:** a new booking starts as **Pending**. The event owner accepts or rejects it, and the user then sees **Confirmed** or **Rejected**. Seat capacity is checked when a booking is requested and again when it is accepted.
- **Private events:** a secret share token is created automatically with the event. Only the owner or people with the link can open it; an empty token never matches.
- **My Bookings page:** see all your bookings and their status, cancel a booking, and manage the events you created (accept or reject requests, share link, edit, delete).
- **Profile page:** update name, email and password.

### For admins
- **Overview:** totals for users, events and bookings.
- **Users:** search, make or remove admin, delete a user (with their events and bookings).
- **Events:** search, filter public or private, delete, and an **+ Add Event** shortcut.
- **Bookings:** search, filter by status, approve or cancel.
- **Site Settings:** change the website name, home page heading and text, dashboard welcome text, footer text and copyright line, without touching the code.
- **Slider:** upload, reorder and remove the home page slider images.

---

## Tech stack

| Part | Technology |
|------|------------|
| Backend | PHP 8 (PDO, prepared statements) |
| Database | MySQL / MariaDB |
| Frontend | HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Bootstrap 5.3 |
| Local server | XAMPP (Apache + MySQL) |

---

## Project structure

```
eventora/
├── index.php            Public landing page (logged-in users go to the dashboard)
├── dashboard.php        User dashboard
├── admin.php            Admin panel (admins only)
├── profile.php          Edit profile and change password
├── events.php           Browse public events
├── event-details.php    Event page and booking request
├── create-event.php     Create an event
├── edit-event.php       Edit an event (owner or admin)
├── booking.php          My bookings, booking requests, events I created
├── login.php            Login (admins go to admin.php, others to dashboard.php)
├── register.php         Sign up
├── logout.php           Log out
├── includes/
│   ├── db.php           Database connection
│   ├── functions.php    Sessions, CSRF, flash messages, helpers
│   ├── header.php       Navbar, CSS links, site settings helpers
│   ├── footer.php       Footer
│   └── event_card.php   Reusable event card
├── CSS/
│   ├── index.css        Main theme (pink palette) loaded on every page
│   ├── common.css       Shared styles loaded on every page
│   └── <page>.css       Optional page styles (home, login, register, events, ...),
│                        loaded automatically when a file matches the page name
├── sql/
│   └── eventora.sql     Full schema and base data (the extra SQL below is already included)
└── pics/
    ├── (default slider and event images)
    ├── uploads/         Event cover images (created automatically on first upload)
    └── slides/          Slider images uploaded from the admin panel (created automatically)
```

